    "result": "Perfect! All tests pass across the entire workspace. Here's a summary of the fixes:\n\n## Issues Fixed\n\n### 1. **Governance Test - Missing Named Exports** \n**File:** `packages/frai-core/src/finetune/index.js`\n\nThe test was importing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but the module only exported it in the default export object. Added named exports for:\n- `APPROVAL_STATUSES`\n- `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`\n- `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`\n- `RISK_LEVELS`\n\nThis maintains backward compatibility since the default export still works.\n\n### 2. **Evaluation Test - Toxicity Metric Misuse**\n**File:** `packages/frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js`\n\nThe `toxicityMetric` function was incorrectly using the `references` parameter as `bannedTerms`. This caused valid outputs to be flagged as toxic because the references were being used as the list of banned keywords.\n\nChanged the function to always use the `defaultBannedTerms` array and ignore the `references` parameter, while maintaining the same function signature for backward compatibility.\n\n## Test Results\n\u2705 **frai-core:** 28 tests passed (8 test files)  \n\u2705 **frai-gate:** 11 tests passed  \n\u2705 **Full workspace:** All tests passing\n\nAll existing public exports remain intact and functional.",
